    "description": "Mine (stage 2, gold), level 2 of 3: L1 plus flourish 2. Over budget: 542 blocks vs 170 (stage 1 alone is 280, mostly its spoil mound). Stage 2 of the mine (gold, tier 5): the approved stage-1 adit and spoil mound, with a 9-tall headframe over a new shaft beside it (stone collar, dark oak legs, deck, sheave and hoist chain). L2 adds an ore-sorting shed, a ladder and a rail spur; L3 a stone gold lockup with an iron door, banners and a sign. The stage-1 flowers that stood on cobblestone now have dirt under them. Builders never dig: miners dig the shaft down from the open cell in the collar. Not yet builder-tested: cauldron, coal_block, ladder, rail, raw_iron_block. Decoration step adds: item, item_frame, minecart.",
